  "usage": {
    "description": "Reaction-diffusion simulations create organic patterns through the interaction of two chemicals (A and B). Different feed/kill rate combinations produce dramatically different patterns. The last preset shows chaining RD with blur and feedback for complex effects.",
    "notes": [
      "Patterns evolve over time - give them 5-10 seconds to stabilize",
      "Random initialization creates unique results each run",
      "Feed and kill rates are highly sensitive - small changes create big differences",
      "Increase timestep for faster evolution (may become unstable)",
      "Use as animated texture source for other effects"
    ]
  }
